Just an aside, when I'm a starting wizard, I'm always _very_ careful
when entering shops.  A few points about mimics:

1. Even if they're mimicing a known object (ie, something other than [),
   that object will not remain on the map when you can't see it.  Enter
   the store, then either put on a blindfold/towel, or leave the store and
   walk around a corner and see if anything disappears.

2. Pets never accidentally walk into a mimic.  Or if they do, you get a
   message like "Your kitten notices a mimic!" or something similar.  So
   don't step where your pet doesn't.

3. If you have a cheap object:  A dart or a rock, for example.  Throw it
   over a row of objects in the store (being careful not to hit the
   shopkeeper).  If there's a mimic in that row, your object will stop,
   and the (first) mimic will be revealed.  Note that the shopkeeper
   will take this as an attempt to sell the object you just threw.

